From 646b12888d2c18938f3a7a2551cff1c93efb9626 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shogo Agent <agent@shogo.ai>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:42:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Day 3: DLD-sourced PSF, N+1 and scraper fixes, Investment
 Score engine
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FIX-07 — PSF provenance is now visible. Community PSF already preferred the DLD
transaction register over listing asking prices and recorded which won in
`psfSource`, but the field never reached the API, so a caller could not tell a
registered price from an asking-price stand-in. It is now in the community list,
the district payload and the score response. On the current database every
community reads `listing` or `none`, because the transaction table is empty
(DLD sync needs DUBAI_PULSE_API_KEY) — a fact the API can now state.

FIX-08 — N+1. The read paths were already batched by an earlier pass; the loops
still awaiting Prisma per iteration were the scraper's, where `ensureCommunity`
issued a findFirst for every one of ~6,000 scraped listings. It is memoised per
run now (cleared at the start of each run so a stale map cannot be inherited).
scripts/find-nplus1.py finds and reports this class of loop.

FIX-09 — the scraper never retried. `fetchWithRetry` adds exponential backoff
with explicit 429/503 handling, and `pfFetchPage` now reports `throttled`
separately from an empty result, so the circuit breaker trips on a refusal
instead of on three genuinely thin areas. The run is wrapped so ScraperLog always
reaches a terminal state, and a stale 'running' row from a killed process is
closed at the start of the next run and by scripts/reconcile-scraperlog.ts.

FEATURE-01 — Investment Score. New append-only InvestmentScore model, an engine
in src/lib/score-engine.ts (30/25/20/15/10 weights), GET /communities/:slug/score
with the paid breakdown gated behind pro, GET /scores, POST /scores/recompute,
and a 03:00-UAE step in the hourly cron.

Two corrections to the brief: its supply-absorption input computed a neutral 50
for "no data" and then multiplied by 2, scoring the least-documented communities
a perfect 100 — that lifted every score to 60 on this database. A missing input
now stays neutral. And a composite built from placeholders is no longer presented
as a measurement: rows record `dataCoverage` and `notes`, and the API returns a
`confidence` band. Today every community scores 50.0 at coverage 0, which the
response states plainly rather than implying 44 real measurements.

Also fixed, found while verifying the scraper end to end: listings were keyed to
the BUILDING slug on the PropertyFinder card, so a single run created 486
communities named after individual towers, all with zero listings and the wrong
emirate. Listings are now attributed to the area being scraped. The 486 rows were
removed (scoped to zero listings + zero transactions + unknown slug; the 44 real
districts and the 30 configured areas were untouched).

Editing the schema regenerated server.tsx and moved the static handlers above the
custom asset-routing region, killing it and blanking the preview. scripts/
fix-server-order.ts repaired it; verify-server-routing caught it (1/8 -> 8/8).

Verified: day1 83, day2 30, day3 18, fixes 41, stream 15, cron 31, intel 27,
routing 8/8; tsc clean on changed files; score/top-scores/communities endpoints
return 200 with the documented shape; preview serves the bundle as JS.

Co-authored-by: Shogo Agent <agent@shogo.ai>
